{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas","id":915544,"title":"Inferno 2E Update Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-16T05:58:14-07:00","id":915544,"title":"Inferno 2E Update Ideas","content":"So I'm rather fond of <b>Inferno</b> 1E book and would want to incprotate in my 2E CoD games. As there is not very much seen in coming material in few next mothes, I got some ideas for using it's demons in current games. To be frank, I come on those when listening <b>Dresden Files <i>Fool Moon</i></b> audiobook in car. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So 2E update ideas:<ul><li>Inferno demons use basic rules of they ephemeral entity they were original ( so previous ghosts, spirits or goetia are using basic 2E mechanics ). Inferno demons get's extra Vice-related Influances called Keys.</li> <li>Inferno demons 'feed' on Breaking Points of cretures around them, especially those related to they Key. What's interesting, no matter what kind of Integrity and related trait it is - Humanity, Wisdom, Clarity, even Harmony. Demons refills they Essence from others making acts related to their Key that leads to Breaking Points. This means that demons tempts mages into making reckless acts in name of their Key and vampire forgets how to be humans by workings of Inferno.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:53:44-07:00","id":915568,"title":"","content":"Ummm..... Two thoughts. First, what do you mean &quot;extra.&quot; Are these going to have additional Influence dots? Because having an Influence of Lust, Pride, etc is already viable.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I'm opposed to tying this to breaking points. Inferno creatures are tied to &quot;acts of evil.&quot; Whatever you define evil as, but its still harmful actions. That's what makes them demonic. Meeting a lustful Daeva and suffering an Integrity breaking point shouldn't feed a demon of Lust. Maybe the vampire's actions could feed the demon, but the mortal's? Not a chance. Mortals tend to suffer breaking points in a Call of Cthulhu manner - &quot;exposure to the supernatural drives you insane.&quot; Completely inappropriate to feed a demon. The Unchained suffer breaking points for exposure - unrelated to &quot;evil.&quot; A werewolf suffering a breaking point to the Flesh for eating a pizza? Even if you say that's gluttony, feeding a demon with that is kinda lame. <br /> <br /> In 1e, we had Morality equivalents. There was a direct tie between Morality equivalents and acting moral. In 2e, you can have low Integrity equivalents and act entirely in a moral and ethical manner. The two are completely unrelated. If you try to tie them together, then we're goign to get into odd situations where a vampire is feeding a demon for living longer than their mortal siblings. And that's just not demonic. You'd be better off looking towards how Beasts fulfill their hunger by moments of shock and loss as inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:06:08-07:00","id":915575,"title":"","content":"I like the thought, and I adore Inferno.<br /> <br /> I also don't think tying them to Breaking Points / Equivalents is a good idea. It is extremely limiting and not entirely in-theme. Unnecessary ties to Breaking Points is my largest gripe with the Social Maneuvering system, we don't need anything else going down that path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:23:42-07:00","id":915588,"title":"","content":"So, I've been thinking about doing a homebrew update to this myself for a while, and one thing I really want to see is a take that allows Whisperers and Diaboli to exist without Dominions. Inferno flirted a lot with the idea that maybe there's actually no such thing as Dominions - Whisperers might just be human nature and Diaboli might just be ephemeral entities that have been corrupted by sin. But it never gave the idea any teeth, and I would like to see a 2e update give that idea some more mechanical weight. Make it possible for Whisperers and Daboli to exist without Dominions and make Dominions entirely optional. Here's how I would do that:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Hearing Whispers is a Persistent Condition that characters can gain instead of the normal Persistent Conditions for Dramatically Failing an Integrity Breaking Point if that Breaking Point played into their Vice.<br /> \u2022 When a character with the Hearing Whispers Condition interacts with an ephemeral entity via the &quot;Interactions with Mortals&quot; or targets one with a supernatural power, there is a chance the mortal will lose the Condition and transfer it to the ephemeral entity.<br /> \u2022 Dominions, if they exist, are a type of ephemeral entity. Their baseline Manifestation Condition is Resonant and their Influences relate to mortal Vices - either specific vices, or means of carrying them out (basically anything that would cl have counted for a Vice or Key in a Malapraxis in 1e). They gain Essence by tempting mortals to indulge in Vices that match their Resonance.<br /> \u2022 Dominions, if they exist, can gain a unique Manifestation called Fall to Whispers that places the Hearing Whispers Condition on a mortal and sends the Dominion into dormancy. The dormant Dominion slumbers inside the being with the Condition (and rides the Condition to any host it is transferred to) until it gains enough Essence to re-form.<br /> \u2022 Infernal Rank, if it exists, is just the Rank of the dormant Dominion riding the Hearing Whispers Condition possessed by an ephemeral entity.<br /> \u2022 Malus Loci, if they exist, are objects or places affected by the Fetter Manifestation Condition tagged to a Dominion.<br /> \u2022 This concept is still a work in progress. Some of these points may change as I develop the idea, and I will likely add more points as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-16-2016, 10:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:44:52-07:00","id":915592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915588#post915588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been thinking about doing a homebrew update to this myself for a while, and one thing I really want to see is a take that allows Whisperers and Diaboli to exist without Dominions. Inferno flirted a lot with the idea that maybe there's actually no such thing as Dominions - Whisperers might just be human nature and Diaboli might just be ephemeral entities that have been corrupted by sin. But it never gave the idea any teeth, and I would like to see a 2e update give that idea some more mechanical weight. Make it possible for Whisperers and Daboli to exist without Dominions and make Dominions entirely optional. Here's how I would do that:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Hearing Whispers is a Persistent Condition that characters can gain instead of the normal Persistent Conditions for Dramatically Failing an Integrity Breaking Point if that Breaking Point played into their Vice.<br /> \u2022 When a character with the Hearing Whispers Condition interacts with an ephemeral entity via the &amp;quot;Interactions with Mortals&amp;quot; or targets one with a supernatural power, there is a chance the mortal will lose the Condition and transfer it to the ephemeral entity.<br /> \u2022 Dominions, if they exist, are a type of ephemeral entity. Their baseline Manifestation Condition is Resonant and their Influences relate to mortal Vices - either specific vices, or means of carrying them out (basically anything that would cl have counted for a Vice or Key in a Malapraxis in 1e). They gain Essence by tempting mortals to indulge in Vices that match their Resonance.<br /> \u2022 Dominions, if they exist, can gain a unique Manifestation called Fall to Whispers that places the Hearing Whispers Condition on a mortal and sends the Dominion into dormancy. The dormant Dominion slumbers inside the being with the Condition (and rides the Condition to any host it is transferred to) until it gains enough Essence to re-form.<br /> \u2022 Infernal Rank, if it exists, is just the Rank of the dormant Dominion riding the Hearing Whispers Condition possessed by an ephemeral entity.<br /> \u2022 Malus Loci, if they exist, are objects or places affected by the Fetter Manifestation Condition tagged to a Dominion.<br /> \u2022 This concept is still a work in progress. Some of these points may change as I develop the idea, and I will likely add more points as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> An interesting way to recycling Dominions could be corrupted souls or corrupted Supernal Entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:47:29-07:00","id":915595,"title":"","content":"Or you could make it that their are no natural Dominions, just Diaboli that have decided to prefect themselves by purifying the none sin parts of themselves, becoming an entity of pure sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:58:18-07:00","id":915606,"title":"","content":"2e does have a mechanic that ties better into &quot;evil&quot; than Breaking Points: Vice. Vice is inherently base-nature, un-good stuff. Have an Inferno Demon feed on people that are getting Willpower back for indulging their Vice, encourage them to do things that would get all their Willpower back. Not sure how to extend this to supernaturals that don't do Virtue/Vice, but you could replace &quot;Vice&quot; with &quot;base nature equivalent&quot; (Dirge, Blood, and Legend rather than Mask, Bone, or Life, for Vampires, Werewolves, and Beasts, respectively).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:59:55-07:00","id":915608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915595#post915595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could make it that their are no natural Dominions, just Diaboli that have decided to prefect themselves by purifying the none sin parts of themselves, becoming an entity of pure sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? Maybe trading out the non-Sin/Vice parts of its Influence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:03:14-07:00","id":915609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915595#post915595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could make it that their are no natural Dominions, just Diaboli that have decided to prefect themselves by purifying the none sin parts of themselves, becoming an entity of pure sin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could do that, but that's not what I want to do. I want to make Dominions completely optional and their existance or nonexistance to be a mystery and a matter of speculation and debate among those in the know about Infernal entities. Just like Inferno implies but fails to follow through on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:12:03-07:00","id":915616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915609#post915609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could do that, but that's not what I want to do. I want to make Dominions completely optional and their existance or nonexistance to be a mystery and a matter of speculation and debate among those in the know about Infernal entities. Just like Inferno implies but fails to follow through on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for what it is worth, Inferno is a liar and tells you so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T08:21:00-07:00","id":915620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915616#post915616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, for what it is worth, Inferno is a liar and tells you so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Haha fair point.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've got some more ideas but I'm on my way to work and won't be able to post except on breaks. I'll write some stuff when I get home. I'm mainly going to focus on the mechanical execution so it doesn't step on any toes regarding what ever folks want the true nature of Infernal entities to be in their games. But one of my design goals is for Whisperers and Diaboli to be able to exist independently of Dominions or to coexist with them according to taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T12:49:37-07:00","id":915773,"title":"","content":"So, I did <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/318864-more-ephemeral-entity-types\">this</a> a while ago - might make a nice stopgap. Just require that the Vices are the Seven Deadly Sins, and you'll be golden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T19:35:51-07:00","id":915978,"title":"","content":"brainstorming some ideas <hr />Demons lack Integrity, Virtue, and Vice. Instead, Demons have a \u201cMalpraxis\u201d, which is the form of Vice, Sin or form of Wickedness that guides the Demons existence. Demons regain Willpower by acting in accordance to their Malpraxis. Most demons have Malpraxis that align with the classic Deadly sins, but others may embody more esoteric or nuanced forms of depravity. A Demon may trade a dot of Influence for an additional Malpraxis.<br /> In addition, all Demons have several potent abilities that are inherent to their nature. Demons understand all languages, even those that are considered lost, dead, or supernatural in nature. No power (mundane or supernatural) can detect a Demons lies, falsehoods and deceptions. Any such ability only reveals the result the demon wants. Lastly, no power or ability can penetrate a demons mind or read its thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence: </b>Demons regain essence when in proximity to an individual indulging behavior that aligns with the Demons Malpraxis, or while in proximity to a suitable condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Diaboli: </b>A Diaboli is an entity that was once a different type of ephemeral creature, but become corrupted into one of the Infernal. Diaboli retain the basic abilities of their original ephemeral type, but lose any pre-existing Integrity, Virtue, or Vice, and gain an appropriate Malpraxis instead. Occults use the terms <i>Deceptors</i> for corrupted Goetia, <i>Immundi</i> for corrupted Spirits, and <i>Larval</i>s for corrupted Ghosts. Theoretically, other ephemeral creatures could become demons \u2013 Angels, Quasmal, Supernal Entities or even Unfettered Beasts could all hear the call of the Inferno. Thankfully no proof of such a thing happening has ever been presented.<br /> <br /> <b>Dominions: </b>Considered \u201ctrue\u201d Demons by occultists, Dominions are native to the Lower Depths. Dominions have a difficult time entering the world, gaining access using the <i>Whisper</i> manifestation, or by being summoned through occult ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>Influence:</b> Demons gain and use Influence in the same way as other ephemeral entities, but most have at least one dot in an Influence related to their Malpraxis.<br /> <br /> <b>Manifestations</b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Realm Gateway:</i></b> The Chronicles of Darkness hold many spiritual realms. Demons know many ways to enter these realms, exploring them for their own reasons. To do so, the Demon must find an appropriate point of ingress, such as a Locus, Avernian Gate, or dormant gate to the Hedge and spend 2 Essence. Each time this power is selected, it is keyed to a specific non-native realm. It may be picked multiple times, once for each realm the Demon would like to access.<br /> <b><i>Whisper:</i></b> A rather than appearing in Twilight Form, a demon with this manifestation may instead appear as a \u201cWhisper\u201d. A demon using this manifestation is wholly insubstantial and invisible, even to other ephemeral beings. A Whisper cannot physically interact with other ephemeral entries in Twilight, but is aware of such beings, regardless of type. The Demon may still make full use of its Influences, but may cannot access any of its Numina. Magic abilities capable of detecting Souls can detect a Whisper.<br /> Dominions begin with Whisper rather than Twilight Form (but may gain it as an additional Manifestation). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T19:46:59-07:00","id":915981,"title":"","content":"Had a thought in regards to Demon's feeding. They gain Essence similar to how Spirits gain Essence, except their tied to the Demon's Vice and Keys, and any Demon that causes a Mortal or Supernatural Creature to suffer a Breaking Point related to said Vice or Keys gains Easence equal to how bad the Breaking Point was?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck 06-16-2016, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T20:05:05-07:00","id":915989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915981#post915981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a thought in regards to Demon's feeding. They gain Essence similar to how Spirits gain Essence, except their tied to the Demon's Vice and Keys, and any Demon that causes a Mortal or Supernatural Creature to suffer a Breaking Point related to said Vice or Keys gains Easence equal to how bad the Breaking Point was?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Discussed, and I think the idea was that tying general feeding to Breaking Points was a bad idea, due to how Integrity and its equivalents are now handled. It's probably better to tie it into a creature's Vice (or Analog). Or just devise a list of what counts for the demon, regardless of their &quot;target&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T20:20:46-07:00","id":915996,"title":"","content":"Still working on this. Gonna take some time before it's ready.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T20:24:43-07:00","id":916001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915989#post915989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Discussed, and I think the idea was that tying general feeding to Breaking Points was a bad idea, due to how Integrity and its equivalents are now handled. It's probably better to tie it into a creature's Vice (or Analog). Or just devise a list of what counts for the demon, regardless of their &quot;target&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I think Infernal entities should feed on Vice, not Breaking Points. However, I do think it's ok for Breaking Points to invite Infernal possession, the logic being that those who have been deeply traumatized or repeatedly exposed to the supernatural are easier targets for Whisperers.<br /> <br /> EDIT: My current thinking is that my take on Dominions will have Vice and Key in place of Virtue and Vice. They will regain a single point of Willpower when they witness another sapient being indulge in their (the Dominion's) Vice, or all Willpower if the act also satisfied their Key. They will gain Dread Powers as well as Manifestations and Numina as they increase in Rank, and one of the sample Dread Powers will grant them an additional Vice or Key and be able to be taken multiple times. I'm thinking of making their baseline Manifestation Condition &quot;Corruption&quot; or &quot;Desecration&quot; instead of Resonance, and that Condition will be caused by the kinds of things Inferno describes as evil acts. Diaboli will be able to treat the Dominion baseline Condition as if it were the appropriate Condition for their base ephemeral entity type. In this way, Infernal entities of all types will seek out mortals with low Integrity to influence, gain Willpower by tempting those morals to indulge in their Vices, and regain Essence by feeding on the resonance created by evil acts those mortals commit, while still keeping Integrity, Vice, and Sin as discrete concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-16-2016, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T00:08:09-07:00","id":916061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915978#post915978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diaboli retain the basic abilities of their original ephemeral type, but lose any pre-existing Integrity, Virtue, or Vice, and gain an appropriate Malpraxis instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>No sense - only ephemeral beings with Integrity, Virtue and Vice are ghosts. And <i>whole charm </i>of ghosts-demons ( like Crowley from <b>Supernatural</b> ) is that they are more human ( i.e. have Integrity and V&amp;V ) than other of those.<br /> <br /> I will not agree to axing Integrity and V&amp;V systems in Inferno demons when they were. Still, much more like word Key than Malpraxis, but it's only term thing for 'source of feeding on bad'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915981#post915981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had a thought in regards to Demon's feeding. They gain Essence similar to how Spirits gain Essence, except their tied to the Demon's Vice and Keys, and any Demon that causes a Mortal or Supernatural Creature to suffer a Breaking Point related to said Vice or Keys gains Easence equal to how bad the Breaking Point was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Was my proposition earlier. I still do not see how it's not gone work with Integrity and Integrity-equivalent rules. <b>Someone can point me where it breaks with those rules? </b>( Beside werewolves - they changing Harmony means it much less battle to sustain it <i>against</i> demons. Still, the Bale Hounds must comes from somewhere... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T00:19:36-07:00","id":916063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916001#post916001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I think Infernal entities should feed on Vice, not Breaking Points.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about <b>Breaking Points <i>through</i> Vice</b>, not Breaking Points all alone or Vice only.<br /> <br /> For Sloth character, it's viable to spend whole evening on couch and get Willpower from this - but I do not see as very demonic to make influence on this. On the other hand - I would also not point demon to get Essence from just making character see something supernatural. However, what I have in mind is like this - Wrath demon induce you to shoot/kill someone in fight or Greed demon influence you to steal new dress from clothing shop - <b>it's your characters Breaking Point but tainted by demons wickedness. <i>Then</i> it will work.</b><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916001#post916001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I do think it's ok for Breaking Points to invite Infernal possession, the logic being that those who have been deeply traumatized or repeatedly exposed to the supernatural are easier targets for Whisperers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention we have exorcisms rules that works on Integrity now, so it's rather logical low Integrity is inviting demons to posses you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T00:34:41-07:00","id":916066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916001#post916001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: My current thinking is that my take on Dominions will have Vice and Key in place of Virtue and Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>And in this very sentence we do not agree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I <i>do not</i> want to strip demon of their previous templates advantages - mechanically ( and story-wise ) all demons were previous members of other ephemera - and they still should work as such. Demon ghosts were ghosts and still should have Integrity ( well, maybe without this one ), and surely Virtue and Vice. Demon spirits should not have Virtue, but Vice only in way of Key, not their own personality per se. Goetia <b>are</b> they own Virtue or Vice so should have those, paired with Key. In the nutshell - leave the basic ephemeral template alone, only <i><b>add</b></i> to it some Inferno corruption parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916001#post916001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They will regain a single point of Willpower when they witness another sapient being indulge in their (the Dominion's) Vice, or all Willpower if the act also satisfied their Key. They will gain Dread Powers as well as Manifestations and Numina as they increase in Rank, and one of the sample Dread Powers will grant them an additional Vice or Key and be able to be taken multiple times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not working with my own aims, but will works for yours.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916001#post916001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this way, Infernal entities of all types will seek out mortals with low Integrity to influence, gain Willpower by tempting those morals to indulge in their Vices, and regain Essence by feeding on the resonance created by evil acts those mortals commit, while still keeping Integrity, Vice, and Sin as discrete concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the heart of our contention - <b>I <i>do not </i>see need for separating those. </b>To me, <i>Breaking Point based on Vice is a Sin</i> - just see any big religion. Shooting to someone in anger - Wrath. Stealing something in needy - Greed. From my reading of <b>Inferno</b> book, <b>it's main idea is that Hell is feeding on breaking/corrupting characters.</b> It want's you to become more unstable, to lower Integrity. <i>Then</i> it can manipulate you, posses you.<br /> <br /> You really do not can make this one without involving somehow Breaking Points with Vice. Other way it will be 'I have Gluttonous character - I get to eat something big in time of work and now I'm posses by demon'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Whole idea of Inferno is that it wants to break your limits, more the better.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T05:55:47-07:00","id":916143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably the heart of our contention - <b>I <i>do not </i>see need for separating those. </b>To me, <i>Breaking Point based on Vice is a Sin</i> - just see any big religion.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIntegrity breaking points are not sins. I'm sorry, but that is not what Integrity represents at all. Integrity represents psychological balance, and its entirely subjective. For someone, self defense killing is a major psychological trauma. For others, revenge killing (such in the case of harming the killer's family) doesn't cause them to lose even a single night's worth of sleep.<br /> <br /> Integrity is not tied to morality. Even with a Vice. That's just not how the system works. Trying to force it is simply not going to work. Even if you argue that murder should be a universal breaking point (I disagree, but lets not digress), that's a whole host of other options out there.<br /> <br /> Also, lots of major religions have different takes on what acting on a Vice is. For a number of them, <i>revenge killing is a virtue.</i> Trying to claim religions as justification is very shaky here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:06:05-07:00","id":916166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in this very sentence we do not agree. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I <i>do not</i> want to strip demon of their previous templates advantages - mechanically ( and story-wise ) all demons were previous members of other ephemera - and they still should work as such. Demon ghosts were ghosts and still should have Integrity ( well, maybe without this one ), and surely Virtue and Vice. Demon spirits should not have Virtue, but Vice only in way of Key, not their own personality per se. Goetia <b>are</b> they own Virtue or Vice so should have those, paired with Key. In the nutshell - leave the basic ephemeral template alone, only <i><b>add</b></i> to it some Inferno corruption parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Wyrd, all <i>Diaboli</i> were previously other types of ephemeral entities. Dominions were a separate thing that came directly from Whisperers that had transcended through Sin. I agree with you that Diaboli shouldn't lose their core template abilities, but I was talking about Dominions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably the heart of our contention - <b>I <i>do not </i>see need for separating those. </b>To me, <i>Breaking Point based on Vice is a Sin</i> - just see any big religion. Shooting to someone in anger - Wrath. Stealing something in needy - Greed. From my reading of <b>Inferno</b> book, <b>it's main idea is that Hell is feeding on breaking/corrupting characters.</b> It want's you to become more unstable, to lower Integrity. <i>Then</i> it can manipulate you, posses you.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Integrity has nothing to do with Sin. Tying Sin to Morality loss made sense in first edition because that was what Morality represented. In second edition, Integrity was completely divorced from that concept and now represents trauma. It still makes sense for Infernal entities to target people with low Integrity, but only because they are easier to manipulate, not because there is anything inherently Sinful about Integrity loss. I'm not separating the ideas, they're already separate in second edition. I'm just trying to fit a concept of Demons that was built around a system with the 7 deadly sins and objective Morality into a system where Vices are personal and the Morality meter has been replaced by a Trauma meter, without making unfortunate implications like the Beast first draft did when it tied Hero creation to Integrity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really do not can make this one without involving somehow Breaking Points with Vice. Other way it will be 'I have Gluttonous character - I get to eat something big in time of work and now I'm posses by demon'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, in my take you only become possessed by a Whisperer when you Dramatically Fail a Breaking Point that got the -1 penalty for acting in accordance with your Vice or a Dominion or Diaboli used Fall to Whispers on you, which would require Desecration as a prerequisite Manifestation Condition. Possession by Dominions and Diaboli would follow the normal ephemeral entity possession rules, which again means having the appropriate prerequisite Condition. The only thing overeating would do is give a Dominion who also has Gluttony as a Vice and sees you do it a point of Willpower. It still needs to tempt you to commit evil acts if it wants to create the Desecration it needs to harvest Essence from, or to break down your Integrity if it wants to make you easier to control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Whole idea of Inferno is that it wants to break your limits, more the better.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Which my take allows for, without conflating trauma with evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-17-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:47:08-07:00","id":916195,"title":"","content":"Questions:<br /> What is the mechanical difference between Malpraxis and the feeding allowed for Resonant conditions anyway <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a>?<br /> So, how do Infernals get Essence with the Vice and Key method <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>?<br /> Mechanically, how do Whispers ascend through Sin <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>? If I might propose, mapping it roughly to the effects of Soul Loss - grind their Integrity and Willpower down.<br /> In what way is Fall to Whispers distinct from Fetter? Both tie you to an creature/object, and both let you use your Influence on them, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:17:56-07:00","id":916215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916195#post916195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how do Infernals get Essence with the Vice and Key method <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure they need to. I think Willpower replenishment is enough incentive for Dominions to influence people to indulge in their Vices. Essence will be regained by staying in Desecrated Conditions, which will give Dominions and Diaboli incentive to influence people to Sin. Since Vice and Sin were the same thing in 1e it made sense for the Malapraxis to replenish both, but I think with 2e's more personal take on Vice, it makes sense to tie Willpower gain to one and Essence gain to the other. I'm open to changing this though, if folks have other suggestions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically, how do Whispers ascend through Sin <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a>? If I might propose, mapping it roughly to the effects of Soul Loss - grind their Integrity and Willpower down.</div> </div> </div> </div>My original thinking was that if Dominions exist, they would be dormant when the Hearing Whispers Condition was active, and &quot;Transcendence through Sin&quot; would merely be the Dominion regaining enough Essence through the Desecrating acts the Whispers encouraged the host to commit that it could reform. If they don't exist, Transcendence through Sin is a myth, and &quot;demons&quot; are just people and ephemeral entities who do bad things under the influence of Whisperers (which again, is just their nature).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916066#post916066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what way is Fall to Whispers distinct from Fetter? Both tie you to an creature/object, and both let you use your Influence on them, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the points that's still very much work in progress. Im not sure if I want Fall to Whispers to be a Manifestaton, a Dread Power, or just to toss it out and say it's just Fetter. That said, I'm leaning away from the third option because in Inferno, Whisperers had almost no actual control over their hosts - certainly less control than the Urged Condition allows for. They could talk to their host and use all manner of psychological trickery to try to get the hosts to listen, but they had no real means of compulsion and in fact relied on mundane social systems. I really want to capture that by tying the Hearing Whispers Condition into Social Maneuvering. Additionally, in Inferno the demon lost access to all but it's most basic powers when it Fell to Whispers. I really like the idea of the power (whether it be a Dread Power or a Manifestation) sending the Dominion or Diabolus into dormancy when used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-17-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:46:50-07:00","id":916245,"title":"","content":"So, here's a thought. Maybe Fall to Whispers isn't a power. Maybe dormant Dominions and Diaboli can cause the Hearing Whispers Condition somehow, and the Fall part is just the Discorporate Manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T08:56:19-07:00","id":916250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916245#post916245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, here's a thought. Maybe Fall to Whispers isn't a power. Maybe dormant Dominions and Diaboli can cause the Hearing Whispers Condition somehow, and the Fall part is just the Discorporate Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would work. Also, if they are Discorporate or even Fettered and dormant, its not like they can use Influence on the target if they don't have the Essence to spare (because they are reconstituting or awakening).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T09:56:58-07:00","id":916285,"title":"","content":"If I might ask, what about the Lores and Testaments? I found that aspect of Demons to be very interesting and unique. <br /> <br /> Actually I suppose you could use the rules of research to create the lore and the summoning rule for crafting a testament.<br /> <br /> Perhaps at a +2 to the target number, much like angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:12:25-07:00","id":916355,"title":"","content":"So many good ideas in this thread - I have wanted to update Inferno for a while but was getting stuck on the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> - Still working on this , but a Malpraxis is used more to define the personality, motives, and behavior of the demon. When it comes to the actual feeding, a target acting out the Demon's Malpraxis is effectively &quot;Resonant&quot; for that kind of sin/vice.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Breaking Points</b><br /> An interesting debate, because I see both sides. Right now I do see the appeal of a essence boost a Demon could receive from a person following their Vice to the breaking point. Even though Vice is no longer explicitly tied to Sin, it still represents ultimately negative and self destructive behavior, and pursuing said Vice even applies a penalty to the Breaking Point roll. I don't see why demons would not be able to gain something from this.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Lores and Testaments </b><br /> The current research and crafting systems do a good job of modeling the work that goes into Demon summoning(and in a bit more elegant fashion than what was presented in Inferno). I will have to take a closer look and do more comparisons to see what Demon-specific embellishments can be added.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:17:35-07:00","id":916357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916166#post916166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which my take allows for, without conflating trauma with evil.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Well, ones 'acts of evil' are traumas to victim. </b>Killing someone? Murder attempt on you should clearly be Breaking Point for most characters. Stealing from someone? Can be Breaking Point for more delicate victim.<br /> <br /> Integrity is still connected to morality - only in much more not clearly way. And open to your society interpretation.<br /> <br /> Also, this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916355#post916355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Breaking Points</b> Even though Vice is no longer explicitly tied to Sin, it still represents ultimately negative and self destructive behavior, and pursuing said Vice even applies a penalty to the Breaking Point roll. I don't see why demons would not be able to gain something from this.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-17-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:23:32-07:00","id":916358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916355#post916355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So many good ideas in this thread - I have wanted to update Inferno for a while but was getting stuck on the mechanics.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> - Still working on this , but a Malpraxis is used more to define the personality, motives, and behavior of the demon. When it comes to the actual feeding, a target acting out the Demon's Malpraxis is effectively &quot;Resonant&quot; for that kind of sin/vice.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Breaking Points</b><br /> An interesting debate, because I see both sides. Right now I do see the appeal of a essence boost a Demon could receive from a person following their Vice to the breaking point. Even though Vice is no longer explicitly tied to Sin, it still represents ultimately negative and self destructive behavior, and pursuing said Vice even applies a penalty to the Breaking Point roll. I don't see why demons would not be able to gain something from this.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Lores and Testaments </b><br /> The current research and crafting systems do a good job of modeling the work that goes into Demon summoning(and in a bit more elegant fashion than what was presented in Inferno). I will have to take a closer look and do more comparisons to see what Demon-specific embellishments can be added.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I wonder if it makes sense for reading/understanding an Infernal's Testament should/could cause the Resonant/Corruption/Desecration Condition. Like, they can sense when you <i>know</i> about them (and feed/harvest Essence from the Condition, as per normal).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916357#post916357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Well, ones 'acts of evil' are traumas to victim. </b>Killing someone? Murder attempt on you should clearly be Breaking Point for most characters. Stealing from someone? Can be Breaking Point for more delicate victim.<br /> <br /> Integrity is still connected to morality - only in much more not clearly way. And open to your society interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, you can have a person for whom murder is <b>not</b> a Breaking Point. It's not &quot;evil&quot; then, nor a sin? Someone can suffer a Breaking Point from someone <i>else's</i> violent outburst. Is the Victim guilty of Wrath by proxy?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916357#post916357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, this:</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more of a dessert thing, rather than the main course, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-17-2016, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:28:04-07:00","id":916360,"title":"","content":"Stories often have demons and witches know when someone says their name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:43:59-07:00","id":916370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916357#post916357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Well, ones 'acts of evil' are traumas to victim. </b>Killing someone? Murder attempt on you should clearly be Breaking Point for most characters. Stealing from someone? Can be Breaking Point for more delicate victim.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can be, but not all Breaking Points are acts of evil on the part of the actor, and not all acts of evil are Breaking Points on the part of the actor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916357#post916357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Integrity is still connected to morality - only in much more not clearly way. And open to your society interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. They coincidentally overlap sometimes, but that doesn't change the fact that Integrity measures ability to cope with trauma, not moral wholesomeness, and Breaking Points are caused by traumatic experiences, not by acts of evil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916357#post916357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, this:</div> </div> </div> </div>Reighnhell is talking about Vice in this quote, not Integrity. You'll notice that in my take, Infernal entities <i>do</i> benefit from influencing people to indulge in Vice. And a Breaking Point roll that was affected by the -1 penalty for acting in accordance with your Vice is <i>how you acquire Whisperers</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T12:55:09-07:00","id":916379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916358#post916358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, you can have a person for whom murder is <b>not</b> a Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where?<br /> <br /> Witnessing a murder \u20133<br /> Committing premeditated murder \u20135<br /> Killing in self-defense \u20134<br /> Killing by accident (car wreck, e.g.) \u20134<br /> Causing visible serious injury to a person \u20132<br /> <br /> But even when murdering is not Breaking Point - so murder-related demons do not choose them as feeding sources. OR they rise the stakes - even your most hardened mercenary will roll on Breaking Point when he will massacre whole village.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916358#post916358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not &quot;evil&quot; then, nor a sin? Someone can suffer a Breaking Point from someone <i>else's</i> violent outburst. Is the Victim guilty of Wrath by proxy?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>What does it matter to the demon who is victim and who is perpetrator?</b> When being on scene of the act, demon just tap to the sources of Vice Essence through Breaking Point - and is the perpetrator losing Breaking Point or victim <i>does not have real meaning to it</i>. Essence is important to it. Who is providing it should not be anything more suitable than 'breaking someone more is giving me more Essence' or 'strategically, this person will make great Hells puppet'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916358#post916358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's more of a dessert thing, rather than the main course, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Inferno demons could be much more gourmets, looking for much more delicacy Essence - that is also suitable to both 1E portray and pop-culture idea of Hell demons. They look for particular taste, corrupting Integrity from Vice actions.<br /> <br /> Once again - I do not think that 'I must eat hot-dog' for Gluttons or 'I spend all day on couch' for Sloth characters are good Inferno demons targets - they do not sound enough... extreme. Adding need for Breaking Points to fulfill Vice action give us nice 'wickedness' feel to demons feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-17-2016, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T06:38:00-07:00","id":916801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916379#post916379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again - I do not think that 'I must eat hot-dog' for Gluttons or 'I spend all day on couch' for Sloth characters are good Inferno demons targets - they do not sound enough... extreme. Adding need for Breaking Points to fulfill Vice action give us nice 'wickedness' feel to demons feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're wrong. Even in 1e the first would have given a demon of Gluttony a point of Willpower through its Malapraxis and the second would have given a demon of Sloth a point of Willpower through its Malapraxis. They regained a point of Essence if the act also satisfied their Key, and all Willpower if the act also triggered a Morality degeneration roll.<br /> <br /> What I am proposing is that they still regain one Willpower for witnessing someone indulge in their Vice (even though Vices can now be things like &quot;cowardly&quot;, &quot;hateful&quot;, or &quot;ambitious&quot; and not just the 7 deadlies), and that also fulfilling the demon's Key would give it back all willpower. Then to regain Essence it would have to spend time in a suitable Condition <i>just like every other ephemeral entity has to do in 2e</i>, and I propose that their suitable Condition should require acts of evil to create, and that it mirror the Desecration system from Inferno.<br /> <br /> Look, I get that you don't think indulging in Vice is severe enough to satisfy a demon (nevermind that it has always been enough to give them back a point of Willpower). But Integrity Breaking Points are simply not a good way to judge increased severity of a Vice. Neither Vice nor Breaking Points relate to sin in Second Edition, so if we're going to update Inferno's demons to 2e, we need to find other ways to measure when characters' actions are suitable for demons to feed off of. Trying to keep it attached to Vice and Breaking Points despite those systems having been changed with the specific intention of making them less related to Christian ideas of sin and evil, is trying to force a square peg into a round hole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 06-18-2016, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T12:12:55-07:00","id":916938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916801#post916801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I get that you don't think indulging in Vice is severe enough to satisfy a demon (nevermind that it has always been enough to give them back a point of Willpower). But Integrity Breaking Points are simply not a good way to judge increased severity of a Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, there's also the small fact that only a minority of players in 2E gamelines are going to have actual Integrity Breaking Points...the less things unnecessarily tied to that system, the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T17:21:52-07:00","id":917052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=916938#post916938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, there's also the small fact that only a minority of players in 2E gamelines are going to have actual Integrity Breaking Points...the less things unnecessarily tied to that system, the better.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they have their own Breaking Points that works with Vice induced idea so much better even. Mage risking his Wisdom on contacts with Inferno is really about not making so defenses to obvious, like sliping his important information in bargains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T17:27:15-07:00","id":917055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917052#post917052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they have their own Breaking Points that works with Vice induced idea so much better even. Mage risking his Wisdom on contacts with Inferno is really about not making so defenses to obvious, like sliping his important information in bargains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harmony doesn't really make sense with this, nor Satiety, nor Cover, nor Clarity, really...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T23:45:09-07:00","id":917206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917055#post917055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Harmony doesn't really make sense with this, nor Satiety, nor Cover, nor Clarity, really...</div> </div> </div> </div>Satiety is not fully Intergrity analog - also Beasts are closes to Inferno demons in first place. God Machine Demons are said to be totally different than Inferno demons. So those two we do not need to concern ourselves.<br /> <br /> Harmony WORKS with this system - just werewolves are <i>very</i> suitable to those changes on spiritual scale. And Forsaken forum points that Harmony as written is much less mobile than many thinks it is, That's why we would have Bale Hounds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Clarity also works with it - changelings are hunted by mad visions of Hell in this take. See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell\">Fearie worse than Hell</a> topic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T02:31:11-07:00","id":917258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917206#post917206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff about Integrity analogs</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems like the only person that would really want this is you. I'd love to see a fully fleshed out system from Charlaquin. Maybe in a different thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T06:55:40-07:00","id":917323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917206#post917206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satiety is not fully Intergrity analog - also Beasts are closes to Inferno demons in first place. God Machine Demons are said to be totally different than Inferno demons. So those two we do not need to concern ourselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says where? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917206#post917206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harmony WORKS with this system - just werewolves are <i>very</i> suitable to those changes on spiritual scale. And Forsaken forum points that Harmony as written is much less mobile than many thinks it is, That's why we would have Bale Hounds. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So... Inferno!Demons are feeding on Werewolves becoming more human? Because Harmony breaks <i>upwards</i> too...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917206#post917206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarity also works with it - changelings are hunted by mad visions of Hell in this take. See <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/908549-faerie-worse-than-hell\">Fearie worse than Hell</a> topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Inferno!Demons feed when a Changeling looses their job, or has to move? Oh, the wickedness! Or the 2E Darkling Seeming Clarity trigger - They risk Clarity by <i>trusting someone</i>. Real evil there...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:39:57-07:00","id":917347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917258#post917258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see a fully fleshed out system from Charlaquin. Maybe in a different thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! That actually might not be a bad idea. It seems Wyrd and I have different design goals for our Inferno updates, and it might be more productive to just make separate threads for developing the different ideas rather than arguing in one thread.<br /> <br /> What do you think, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>? If this discussion is derailing from your goal of brainstorming Inferno update ideas I am fine with starting a separate thread for my updates (honestly it's getting to the point where I could probably benefit from one of those nifty homebrew hub threads like some folks have in their signatures anyway). Or, if you think this discussion is valuable to your purposes I can stick around in this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T08:36:11-07:00","id":917370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917347#post917347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you think, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>? If this discussion is derailing from your goal of brainstorming Inferno update ideas I am fine with starting a separate thread for my updates (honestly it's getting to the point where I could probably benefit from one of those nifty homebrew hub threads like some folks have in their signatures anyway). Or, if you think this discussion is valuable to your purposes I can stick around in this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably will be best - I hate to disagree with you, but I cannot see your reasons and you cannot see mine. It will be more healthy to have other idea on it. Even when I would steal large part of your Conditions, but main ideas we have different. Probably I even start my own topic on clean start on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T09:24:01-07:00","id":917390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917370#post917370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably will be best - I hate to disagree with you, but I cannot see your reasons and you cannot see mine. It will be more healthy to have other idea on it. Even when I would steal large part of your Conditions, but main ideas we have different. Probably I even start my own topic on clean start on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha it's cool, you're welcome to steal my Conditions, or any other parts of my version that you'd like to use <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Since you're planning to post it publicly, I'd appreciate if you credit me on anything you borrow from my version and I'll do the same if I end up borrowing any of yours. Maybe we should leave this thread for general Inferno brainstorming. When I've got enough of my writeup worked out I'll start my own thread for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T01:11:53-07:00","id":917860,"title":"","content":"Add Demons who consume child innocence and attack children. As the servants of Demagogue in Little Fears including their kingdoms .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T03:58:14-07:00","id":917927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917860#post917860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add Demons who consume child innocence and attack children.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would nicely work as demons Essence feeding on Breaking Points 'innocents' have generally high Integrity levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T08:10:58-07:00","id":918046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917323#post917323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Says where? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So... Inferno!Demons are feeding on Werewolves becoming more human? Because Harmony breaks <i>upwards</i> too...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, Inferno!Demons feed when a Changeling looses their job, or has to move? Oh, the wickedness! Or the 2E Darkling Seeming Clarity trigger - They risk Clarity by <i>trusting someone</i>. Real evil there...</div> </div> </div> </div> Hahaha. That's funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T12:21:00-07:00","id":919859,"title":"","content":"So, quick update on my version. I've got a Hearing Whispers Condition and a Desecrated Condition worked out, but I don't want to reveal them before I've ironed out some of the other systems that interact with them. Hearing Whispers is also no longer going to apply to ephemeral entities. Instead, I'm working on a mechanism by which a character with Hearing Whispers can shed the Condition and give a Condition I'm currently calling Diabolical to an ephemeral entity. The Diabolical Condition is what makes ordinary ephemeral entities into Diaboli. I'm also making the baseline Manifestation Condition for Dominions &quot;Corrupted&quot;, which will be similar to Resonant but specifically related to sin, and Desecrated is going to be a Manifestation Condition that applies on top of Anchor, Resonant, Inferastructure, or Corrupted. Kind of like a parallel advancement to Open. I'm currently thinking that Diabolical and Desecrated are going to do a lot of the heavy lifting in this system, causing normal Manifestations to work differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T21:04:34-07:00","id":920128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=915575#post915575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the thought, and I adore Inferno.<br /> <br /> I also don't think tying them to Breaking Points / Equivalents is a good idea. It is extremely limiting and not entirely in-theme. Unnecessary ties to Breaking Points is my largest gripe with the Social Maneuvering system, we don't need anything else going down that path.</div> </div> </div> </div>While this is a valid opinion, since it is a matter of taste, I completely disagree and love the original poster's idea about feeding on breaking points of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:29:32-07:00","id":920175,"title":"","content":"Full disclosure, my system <i>does</i> tie in with Breaking Points, and in more ways that just making someone a candidate for Hearing Whispers. It's just that Dominions and Diaboli don't directly gain Essence from watching people experience Breaking Points, because they're supposed to feed on sin and Breaking Points =/= sin in Second Edition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T22:43:35-07:00","id":920182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=917323#post917323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... Inferno!Demons are feeding on Werewolves becoming more human? Because Harmony breaks <i>upwards</i> too...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, Inferno!Demons feed when a Changeling looses their job, or has to move? Oh, the wickedness! Or the 2E Darkling Seeming Clarity trigger - They risk Clarity by <i>trusting someone</i>. Real evil there...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since all those listed breaking points can easily leave the person with the Guilty condition, why is it less thematically correct for demons to be nurished by people becoming consumed with guilt, being broken or falling into madness? You jest with sarcastic tone in your post, but what if damaging souls/reducing people to ruined versions of themselves is the business of Inferno!Demons? Wouldn't breaking points be exactly the type of trauma they'd want?<br /> <br /> now I use an Atrocity system updated from Dance Macabre along with a modified Hell is other people version of breaking point and intergrated my Inferno!Demons into that, all of which is in the link of the Frailty Chronicles in my signature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-24-2016, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T23:04:15-07:00","id":920192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=920182#post920182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since all those listed breaking points can easily leave the person with the Guilty condition, why is it less thematically correct for demons to be nurished by people becoming consumed with guilt, being broken or falling into madness? You jest with sarcastic tone in your post, but what if damaging souls/reducing people to ruined versions of themselves is the business of Inferno!Demons? Wouldn't breaking points be exactly the type of trauma they'd want?</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't be the demons presented in Infrerno. Those demons don't feed on guilt, &quot;madness&quot;, or trauma, they feed on sin. Now, there's nothing <i>wrong</i> with a different take on demons that do feed on trauma, but that's not what Inferno sold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=920182#post920182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">now I use an Atrocity system updated from Dance Macabre along with a modified Hell is other people version of breaking point and intergrated my Inferno!Demons into that, all of which is in the link of the Frailty Chronicles in my signature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, see that makes sense. You're working with a modified version of Morality, so demons feeding on Breaking Points in your games would to fit the themes of Inferno better than it would for those of us using Integrity as presented in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T03:11:06-07:00","id":920272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/915544-inferno-2e-update-ideas?p=920182#post920182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since all those listed breaking points can easily leave the person with the Guilty condition, why is it less thematically correct for demons to be nurished by people becoming consumed with guilt, being broken or falling into madness? You jest with sarcastic tone in your post, but what if damaging souls/reducing people to ruined versions of themselves is the business of Inferno!Demons? Wouldn't breaking points be exactly the type of trauma they'd want?<br /> <br /> now I use an Atrocity system updated from Dance Macabre along with a modified Hell is other people version of breaking point and intergrated my Inferno!Demons into that, all of which is in the link of the Frailty Chronicles in my signature.</div> </div> </div> </div>And *if* demons fed on the ruin of souls, that would be valid. But they feed on sin, as currently stated.<br /> <br /> Now if you recast them to feed on ruined souls, and sin/vice is merely their preferred tool for inflicting damage (reasonable, considering it makes the Breaking Point roll more difficult), *that* works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}